  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-10 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Marketing (BA/BS) program page and its linked official degree map, 'Marketing Degree Maps (2026-2027)', Marketing (Campus) tab, last updated/reviewed July 27, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. Collected as the B.S.: the catalog prints a single combined line, Total Credits, BA/BS Degree: 120, which the map matches exactly; the map expressly does not include the B.A.'s 16-credit foreign-language requirement. Every semester's courses sum to the map's printed semester total (16/14/15/15/15/15/15/15) and the plan to 120. Cross-check: the catalog's Marketing Curriculum totals 74.5 credits (Pre-Business Foundation 23, Additional Business Foundation 9, Business Core 18.5 including the 0.5-credit BA 4999 Assurance of Learning, Marketing Core 24), and every named curriculum course appears in the map, including the Marketing Core's three-course choice (9 credits), which the map fills with two MKTG upper-division elective slots and one major upper-division elective slot. Two catalog-versus-map differences are transcribed as printed in the map and disclosed here, not reconciled: the catalog lists the selling course as SALE 2930 Fundamentals of Selling - Building Blocks for Successful Selling, while the map prints MKTG 2930 Fundamentals of Selling in Year 2 Fall; and the catalog lists MKTG 4950 Marketing Management in the Marketing Core, while the map prints MKTG 4850 Marketing Management in Year 4 Spring. Titles follow the map. GE and elective rows printed without course codes are recorded as choice slots with synthetic codes.",
